# CapitalForge Coding Standards

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Files (backend) | kebab-case | `strategy.service.ts` |
| Files (frontend pages) | kebab-case dir | `app/strategy/page.tsx` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `StrategyService` |
| Interfaces/Types | PascalCase | `CreateAllocationDto` |
| Functions/methods | camelCase | `recalculateBuckets()` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `DEFAULT_DCA_WEEKS` |
| DB tables | snake_case | `strategy_rules` |
| Enums | PascalCase values | `TransactionType.BUY` |
| React components | PascalCase | `AppShell` |

## File Organization

### Backend module structure
```
domain/
├── domain.module.ts
├── domain.controller.ts
├── domain.service.ts
└── dto/
    └── domain.dto.ts
```

### Frontend structure
```
app/<route>/page.tsx     # Page component
components/ui/           # shadcn primitives only
components/layout/       # Shell, nav
lib/api.ts               # All HTTP
lib/types.ts             # Shared types
contexts/                # React contexts
```

## Clean Code Rules

- **Thin controllers** — HTTP only, logic in services
- **Single responsibility** — one reason to change per file
- **No dead code** — remove unused imports, variables, functions
- **No magic numbers** — use named constants (e.g., `DEFAULT_CORE_RATIO = 0.60`)
- **Early returns** — guard clauses over deep nesting
- **Max function length** — ~40 lines; extract if longer
- **DRY within module** — don't duplicate across modules unless shared in `common/`

## Documentation Requirements

- **Self-documenting code** preferred over comments
- Comment only: non-obvious business logic, Excel formula references, workarounds
- JSDoc on public service methods that cross modules
- Update `API_CONTRACTS.md` when adding/changing endpoints
- No README changes unless explicitly requested

## Error Handling Standards

### Backend
```typescript
throw new NotFoundException(`Portfolio ${id} not found`);
throw new BadRequestException('Bucket ratios must sum to 1.0');
```
- Use NestJS built-in exceptions
- Global filter handles formatting
- Never expose stack traces to client in production

### Frontend
```typescript
try {
  await strategyApi.generate(portfolioId);
  toast.success('Strategy generated');
} catch (error) {
  toast.error('Failed to generate strategy');
}
```
- User-friendly messages in UI
- 401 handled by axios interceptor (redirect to login)

## Logging Standards

```typescript
private readonly logger = new Logger(ClassName.name);
this.logger.log('Operation started');
this.logger.warn('Degraded: using cached prices');
this.logger.error('Failed', error.stack);
```

**Never log:** passwords, JWT tokens, DATABASE_URL, user PII beyond userId

## TypeScript Standards

- Strict mode enabled
- No `any` unless unavoidable — prefer `unknown` + type guard
- DTOs with class-validator decorators on all inputs
- Shared types in `frontend/src/lib/types.ts` matching backend DTOs

## Money Handling

```typescript
import { Decimal } from '@prisma/client/runtime/library';
// Always Decimal for money — never Number()
```

## Import Order

1. External packages (`@nestjs/*`, `react`)
2. Internal modules (`../allocation/`)
3. Relative imports (`./dto/`)
4. Types (`import type { ... }`)
